{
 "priority": 7,
 "source_bins": [
  "talk.bin"
 ],
 "strings": {
  "Do you want to go outside and get some fresh air?": "",
  "...Yeah, I'll take you up on that.": "",
  "Great. Let's put that brain of yours to work, then!": "",
  "Nice. It opened.": "",
  "Incredible! Yagami-san from Cloudy Skies Publishing has done it again!": "",
  "The digits of the multiplication answers formed our answer, \"3412\"!": "",
  "Impressive. It looks like Cloudy Skies will be getting two of my books.": "",
  "You're really something, Yagami-san. Next time I'll have to do better.": "",
  "(Uh... Next time?)": "",
  "You're a genius, Yagami-san!": "",
  "We can head back whenever you're ready.": "",
  "Feeling refreshed, Yagami-san? Do you want to go back?": "",
  "Just a sec, actually.": "",
  "Thank you again, Yagami-san. You're an incredible detective.": "",
  "Ha, it was dumb luck. If I was so amazing, I'd be getting more cases.": "",
  "You're much too modest! You pulled this off twice in a row, and that can't be a coincidence!": "",
  "I'm just glad I could help.": "",
  "Thank you very much. Here's your fee. You've earned it!": "",
  "I have much to discuss with Katagiri-sensei, so I'll head off!": "",
  "(But why did he say there'd be a next time...)": "",
  "Great! I think we've got this third book in the bag!": "",
  "What part of this is \"we\"...": "",
  "Thank you all for attending, everyone. I think we all know the drill by now, yes?": "",
  "However before we begin, Katagiri-sensei has a few words.": "",
  "Please, Sensei.": "",
  "First, let me extend my most heartfelt thanks that you would all come out to this for a third time.": "",
  "Believe me when I say I have never felt so creatively energized, and I have completed a third book!": "",
  "But it's important to me that I keep the playing field level, and so, I've devised another problem.": "",
  "I believe this novel could very well be my magnum opus, and I can't wait for you all to read it.": "",
  "(...I'm starting to wonder which one he likes better, writing books or problems...)": "",
  "As usual, he who solves the problem, wins the publishing rights.": "",
  "I look forward to your efforts, everyone. Thank you.": "",
  "His best work ever, huh? I bet he's come up with a near impossible problem...": "",
  "We're ready to announce the problem, but in case you've forgotten the rules, here they are, real quick!": "",
  "The problem will result in an answer that opens the safe on this stage!": "",
  "Inside the safe, is the sensei's master script!": "",
  "If you have a solution ready, just come up and try your luck on the safe!": "",
  "If it opens, you've earned the rights to Katagiri-sensei's newest novel!": "",
  "With that, are you ready? Here's the problem!": "",
  "...What does it even mean? I'm so confused.": "",
  "(Okay, let's think about this...)": "",
  "(6 + 2 and 9 - 5 is just what you'd think. But if 1 + 11 becomes 0...)": "",
  "(That means the rules change at 12. What's something that goes from 1 to 12?)": "",
  "(Oh. Duh.)": "",
  "I think... I've got it.": "",
  "The genius detective strikes again! Go ahead and open the safe, Yagami-san!": "",
  "Yeah, I'm on it.": "",
  "Oh, once again it's Yagami-san of Cloudy Skies Publishing!": "",
  "Are you as confident as you have been before, Yagami-san?": "",
  "Well, this was a hard one, but I think I figured it out.": "",
  "Well, you certainly have a track record for it! Go ahead, Yagami-san!": "",
  "(Alright, time to enter the code.)": "",
  "(It changes when it becomes 12... Something from 1 to 12...)": "",
  "Ah, it looks like that's incorrect.": "",
  "(Huh? ...Guess I got sidetracked. I'll have to rethink this.)": "",
  "Don't give up, Yagami-san! Keep trying!": "",
  "...I know, I will.": "",
  "Would you like to go outside and get some fresh air?": "",
  "Hey, it opened.": "",
  "Wow! Yagami-san and Cloudy Skies Publishing have solved the riddle yet again!": "",
  "This problem is represented by a clock, of course. If you add three hours to 5:00, it becomes 8:00.": "",
  "But if you subtract ten hours from 7:00, it becomes 9:00. And if you add eleven hours to 3:00, then you've got 2:00.": "",
  "Finally, subtract seven hours from midnight, you get 5:00. This makes the answer 8925.": "",
  "It seems I just can't stump you, Yagami-san.": "",
  "Ha, I'm sure you'd eventually get me.": "",
  "Cloudy Skies Publishing has won the rights to my third book, and yet, I have to ask...": "",
  "Why haven't you published the two you had already?": "",
  "Um, because...": "",
  "Because I believe these three books constitute a trilogy, Katagiri-sensei!": "",
  "Oh, Kawada-san.": "",
  "I could tell when I read them. Parts one and two seem too incomplete to exist on their own.": "",
  "I suspect that the mystery is only solved once you've read the third and final part!": "",
  "So I could never bring myself to publish an unsolved mystery!": "",
  "...Wonderful! I'm so glad you caught on.": "",
  "I've actually been thinking about hanging up the proverbial pen and retiring. I've felt rather galled by this industry.": "",
  "Galled, Sensei?": "",
  "Ever since I became a best-selling author, the industry has put my name on a pedestal.": "",
  "They didn't care what I wrote. I could write garbage, and they would take it as long as it said, \"Takumi Katagiri.\"": "",
  "The first reader is the editor, wouldn't you say? But they weren't even reading my content!": "",
  "That's what led me to resort to measures like this.": "",
  "First, I wanted a test that would measure a publisher's ability to truly comprehend mystery novels.": "",
  "But the true test was exactly as you've discovered. I hid the fact that it was a trilogy.": "",
  "S-So if we'd gone ahead and published the first or second books...": "",
  "I would have revoked the rights, hidden away the third book, and retired from the public eye.": "",
  "Thankfully, none of that came to pass. Cloudy Skies Publishing has passed with flying colors.": "",
  "You are exactly who I want to work with for the rest of my days. I will sign exclusive publishing rights to you.": "",
  "...Huh? E-E-Exclusive? You mean that?": "",
  "Yes, I do.": "",
  "I-I'm... I'm so honored!": "",
  "Let me know when you're ready. We'll head back.": "",
  "Thank you so much, Yagami-san. I think our company is completely safe now.": "",
  "It's your own doing, you know. You have a real editor's eye.": "",
  "Hahaha, I'm still in shock, to be frank.": "",
  "Well, I'm sure you and that author are going to get along great.": "",
  "Yes, I hope so!": "",
  "Here's your payment. Thank you again.": "",
  "No, thank you.": "",
  "Keep an eye on the bookshelves, Yagami-san! Next time we meet, I promise to have good news!": "",
  "Haha, looking forward to it.": "",
  "Great! I'll be seeing you, then!": "",
  "(I haven't curled up with a good book in a long time. I oughta do that.)": "",
  "Hello, Kawada-san. How are you?": "",
  "Oh, fine, thank you. Thank you so much for all your help lately.": "",
  "Not at all. How are your books selling?": "",
  "Two books at the same time from a famous author must have made waves, right?": "",
  "Well, actually... We still haven't published them.": "",
  "What!? You don't mean...": "",
  "I'm afraid so. This is a trilogy we're dealing with.": "",
  "He did say something about a \"next time\" when I solved his last problem...": "",
  "Did he? He's a crafty devil...": "",
  "But I've read the second novel cover to cover, and there's so many loose ends...": "",
  "There's no way to solve the mystery! Which is why I think the third and final book will be the key...": "",
  "But I could never publish it as an incomplete trilogy!": "",
  "So let me guess what we have to do...": "",
  "You got it! Another problem event!": "",
  "We need this to complete the set, Yagami-san!": "",
  "Okay, but couldn't you start with the first two?": "",
  "I thought your company was in danger of going under.": "",
  "You're not seeing the big picture, Yagami-san! If we published an incomplete trilogy, readers would be furious!": "",
  "This trilogy has to be published together or the whole mystery loses its integrity!": "",
  "Huh. So you're actually putting the quality of the experience over the sales numbers.": "",
  "Well, I can't say this isn't stretching us thinner than I'd ever imagined...": "",
  "But I love books too much to gamble on publishing something that would tarnish the story.": "",
  "I see... I can appreciate that.": "",
  "Listen. I'll pay you even more than last time. How about 380,000 yen?": "",
  "Fine. But I'm only taking it if I can pull this off again, somehow.": "",
  "That's okay! I have faith in you, Yagami-san!": "",
  "Shall we, then? Are you ready?": "",
  "Yagami-san! So we meet again.": "",
  "You're that journalist from before...": "",
  "The name's Hiranuma, and I'm actually just a freelancer now. But that's neither here nor there.": "",
  "Sorry to throw this at you, but I hear you're not only a detective, but also a jack-of-all-trades. Is that right?": "",
  "Not sure where you heard that, but I'll take a case as long as it's up my alley. Most of the time.": "",
  "I see. Then I have a job for you. I need you to take some pictures of a certain someone.": "",
  "I'll be compensating you, of course. How does 50,000 yen sound?": "",
  "That does sound nice... but not right now.": "",
  "I see. Well, if you do ever have some time on your hands, let me know what's good.": "",
  "That'd be nice. Who's this certain someone you need pictures of?": "",
  "You know Kotatsu Higurashi, right? The guy who framed Horny Hinata. He's apparently been on hiatus ever since that whole fiasco.": "",
  "So I need you to get me his picture.": "",
  "What could you possibly do with that, though...?": "",
  "Well, apparently he's going through some hard times. Heard his agency's been keeping him from appearing on TV and such.": "",
  "And since he can't land gigs on his own, he resorted to pestering customers on Senryo Avenue as a barker.": "",
  "Frankly, I thought that sounded pretty funny, so I want to see it for myself.": "",
  "He's really fallen down the hole, hasn't he?": "",
  "Yep. Maybe he thought it'd be easier to pull people in, given his fifteen minutes of fame. If you could call it that.": "",
  "But anyway, would you mind helping me out? Try to get as close as you can.": "",
  "Yagami-san, you're back. Care to lend a hand?": "",
  "Sorry, I'm a little slammed.": "",
  "(Ah, here he is...)": "",
  "Hey buddy! Yeah, you, over there! Wanna see some voluptuous vixens today? Looks like you could use the attention!": "",
  "Huh? Isn't that... Higurashi?": "",
  "Hey, Higurashi! Do that thing you always do! You know, with your eyeballs!": "",
  "Ya wanna see me do something with balls, huh...?": "",
  "Then how 'bout I whip out my dangly, leathery <font_kind=yakuza_italic>sack</font_kind> and then we'll see who's laughing!": "",
  "Ugh... Let's get out of here. His new material is terrible.": "",
  "Yeah, you've really gone off the deep end... And to think I felt sorry for you.": "",
  "What...!? Fine then, get outta here! Buncha cheapshits!": "",
  "(Wow, he really has no shame, does he? I doubt he'll be making a comeback anytime soon.)": "",
  "Well, time to get that photo! I need to get as close as I can.": "",
  "(Hmm... I should take a picture.)": "",
  "(Hmm. Can't really tell who's in there...)": "",
  "(Gotta get his whole body next time...)": "",
  "(Hah, nailed it. Now that's a solid picture.)": "",
  "(Guess it's back to Shellac for me.)": "",
  "Hiranuma-san. I believe you wanted this?": "",
  "And Yagami-san delivers the goods! That was fast.": "",
  "Yeah, I can definitely use this... I can almost see the headline already!": "",
  "Here's a little something for your trouble.": "",
  "Well, looks like it's back to the office for this guy! Thanks!": "",
  "Sure thing. Let me know if you ever need any more help.": "",
  "Yagami-san, my main man!": "",
  "Hey, Hiranuma-san. You come by Shellac pretty often, I see.": "",
  "Eh. I do when I feel like getting hammered.": "",
  "...Which is gonna need to happen after this next job. You up for playing photographer again?": "",
  "Sure, but what kinda job are we talking about?": "",
  "I need you to take some pictures again.": "",
  "This time, it's a performing artist who was on the news recently because of some kind of scandal.": "",
  "His stage name's Bram-sama. Have you heard of him? He's one of those goth rockers with a vampire persona.": "",
  "Yeah, let's just say I'm... familiar.": "",
  "Good, this'll go a lot quicker.": "",
  "He's apparently doing community service to make amends for something he did in the past.": "",
  "And since I want to write an article about it, I need you to get his picture.": "",
  "Yeah, that whole thing... Did you catch that press interview that aired with him?": "",
  "Hm? No, not really. Why, do you know something about it?": "",
  "Huh? Oh. Nah.": "",
  "(Nobody's ever going to know that was me... What a relief.)": "",
  "(Although, I was half-tempted to spill it just now. Maybe someday...)": "",
  "Anyway, I hear Bram-sama has been picking up trash around town as part of his community service.": "",
  "Yeah, he got off light. But if you ask me, even though he whines, at least he takes it seriously.": "",
  "I'm surprised he's actually going through with it.": "",
  "I've been rather curious about that myself.": "",
  "That's why I wanted you to check on him and see how he was handling it. With photo evidence, of course.": "",
  "Apparently he picks up trash near Park Boulevard pretty often. Would fifty g's get you to do it?": "",
  "Say no more. I'm on the case.": "",
  "(Oh boy, here we go...)": "",
  "What wretched scoundrel would dare discard this object without so much as a passing thought!?": "",
  "I'll help you pick it up, Bram-sama!": "",
  "No. Prostrate thyself no further, human. For I, Bram-sama, must bear this cross of atonement alone.": "",
  "Yet, if you still wish to lend me your aid... then I give you a single command!": "",
  "Here it comes... He's gonna say his catchphrase!": "",
  "Ahhh! ❤ Bram-sama, we love youuu!": "",
  "(Even when he's picking up trash, he finds a way to work that in. Impressive.)": "",
  "Okay. Time to get that picture.": "",
  "(Mm. No good. It's hard to tell what he's doing.)": "",
  "Hiranuma-san, I got it. Here, it's Bram-sama.": "",
  "Oh, thanks, Yagami-san.": "",
  "Huh. This picture's actually kinda nice. Tasteful, even... Don't ask me why, it just is. Makes for good writing.": "",
  "Here. For a job well done.": "",
  "I should be the one thanking you. You were definitely the man for the job.": "",
  "Hope we can work together again.": "",
  "Yeah, I'll see what I can do.": "",
  "Thanks again. I'll contact you again if I ever need some help.": "",
  "Sure, but what kinda photo are we talking about this time?": "",
  "Hey, Yagami-san. You think you can get some photos for me again?": "",
  "A crow.": "",
  "It's not just any ordinary crow—I'm looking for the rare and fabled <color=keyword>white crow</color>.": "",
  "A crow... What for?": "",
  "At first, I couldn't believe it either. But then all these witnesses started showing up, so I figured it might be real.": "",
  "I bet people would lose their minds if they happened to see it for themselves.": "",
  "A white crow? Not sure I'm buying that.": "",
  "Rare doesn't even begin to describe it.": "",
  "(This would be one of the higher spots in town.)": "",
  "Oh! There it is!": "",
  "It really is all by itself... and at night, too... Kinda sad.": "",
  "Well. Time to take its picture before it flies off somewhere.": "",
  "All right. Maybe I should get into nature photography!": "",
  "...But can you even tell this is a white crow? It could easily pass for a dove or a seagull...": "",
  "Oh well. Let's just take this over to Hiranuma-san for now.": "",
  "Hiranuma-san. I brought you the picture you asked for.": "",
  "Whoa, you actually <font_kind=yakuza_italic>found</font_kind> the dang bird? Let's see it!": "",
  "This'll make headlines for sure! Way to go, Yagami-san!": "",
  "But can you actually tell it's a white crow?": "",
  "Nope! The fact that we don't know for sure is what makes it so great! That's how curiosity is born!": "",
  "Think about it. We're talking about a rare white crow that struggles to make it past infancy, here in the middle of Tokyo.": "",
  "Having only been confirmed in eyewitness accounts and vague photographs, it's something of a local phenomenon.": "",
  "Oh, I get it. Kind of like Nessie or Bigfoot?": "",
  "Exactly! Whenever there's an unsolved mystery, people get swept up in the adventure.": "",
  "\"A solitary white crow cuts through the night sky, high above a city where outcasts gather. Fact or fiction? You decide.\"": "",
  "Ah. When you put it that way, I do kinda get a sense of adventure.": "",
  "Right? With so much negativity on the news these days, the world needs this sort of thing. Spreads some hope, you know?": "",
  "Well, I'll be damned. So you're not just chasing scandal after scandal. This might actually cheer people up.": "",
  "Haha, well, I just did this on a whim. I'm probably better off chasing celebrities anyway.": "",
  "Here. Take this as your payment for today.": "",
  "Hey, thank you for getting me all these amazing photos. We should work together again whenever we get the chance.": "",
  "Definitely. This has been working out pretty well for the both of us.": "",
  "Haha, so it seems. Two professionals cast out by the profession that made them. What are the odds, huh?": "",
  "In some poetic way, we're the white crows of our careers. Though not quite as rare.": "",
  "Haha. Guess that's the way it goes.": "",
  "Well then. Hope to see you around.": ""
 },
 "ref_tm": {
  "Yes, I do.": "ครับ ผมเข้าใจครับ",
  "No, thank you.": "ไม่ล่ะ ขอบคุณนะ",
  "(Oh boy, here we go...)": "(โอ๊ย มาอีกละ...)",
  "Yeah, I'll see what I can do.": "ได้ ฉันจะลองดูว่าช่วยอะไรได้บ้าง"
 }
}
